CSRF Token Location & Usage in LEAF
Based on repository analysis, here's exactly where and how LEAF's CSRF token lives:

1. Backend Generation (PHP)
The token is generated in the PHP session:

PHP
public function generateCSRFToken()
{
    $_SESSION['CSRFToken'] = bin2hex(random_bytes(32));
}
Location: LEAF_Nexus/sources/Login.php
Stored in: $_SESSION['CSRFToken'] (server-side session variable)

2. Frontend Rendering
LEAF uses two primary methods to expose the token on the rendered page:

Method A: Hidden Form Input (most common)
HTML
<input name="CSRFToken" type="hidden" value="<!--{$CSRFToken}-->" />
Selector: input[name="CSRFToken"]
Examples in templates:

LEAF_Nexus/templates/ajaxForm.tpl
LEAF_Nexus/templates/file_form.tpl
Method B: Global JavaScript Variable
In Smarty templates, the token is also injected as a plain JS variable:

JavaScript
var CSRFToken = '<!--{$CSRFToken}-->';
Variable name: window.CSRFToken (or just CSRFToken in scope)
Examples:

LEAF_Nexus/admin/templates/mod_system.tpl
LEAF_Nexus/scripts/batchRefreshEmployees.php
No cookie: The token is NOT stored as an HTTP cookie, only in the session and DOM.

3. How Frontend Code Reads & Attaches the Token
Pattern: Reading from hidden input
JavaScript
// From form submission or jQuery:
var token = $('input[name="CSRFToken"]').val();
Pattern: Reading from global variable
JavaScript
var token = CSRFToken;  // Direct reference
Pattern: Attaching to AJAX requests
JavaScript
$.ajax({
    type: 'POST',
    url: './api/position/' + positionID,
    data: {
        empUID: empUID,
        CSRFToken: CSRFToken  // Passed as POST data parameter
    },
    success: function(response) { ... }
});
Real example from view_position.tpl:

JavaScript
$.ajax({
    type: 'POST',
    url: './api/position/<!--{$positionID}-->/employee',
    data: {
        empUID: empUID,
        isActing: $('#isActing').prop('checked') ? 1 : 0,
        CSRFToken: '<!--{$CSRFToken}-->'  // Inline Smarty template output
    },
    success: function(response) { ... }
});
Backend Validation
The backend validates POST requests:

PHP
if ($_POST['CSRFToken'] != $_SESSION['CSRFToken'])
{
    return;  // Silently reject if token doesn't match
}
Location: LEAF_Request_Portal/sources/Form.php (and multiple API endpoints)

Summary for Your Bookmarklet/Console Script
To read the CSRF token on leaf.va.gov:

JavaScript
// Primary method: hidden input
const token = document.querySelector('input[name="CSRFToken"]').value;

// Fallback method: global JS variable (if available)
const token = window.CSRFToken;
To use it in requests:

JavaScript
fetch('./api/endpoint', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: new URLSearchParams({
        CSRFToken: token,
        otherParam: 'value'
    })
});
Note: The token varies per session and is regenerated on login. It's stored only in the PHP session and rendered into the DOM as needed—there's no global cookie to intercept.
